{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["Then Moshe set apart — why did he interrupt the words of Moshe, which are connected one to another, and write this deed in between? Rather, because he had spoken at length until now, and now begins to explain the commandments — how he made this Torah clear. And he needs to say in 'Judges and officers': three cities you shall set apart for yourself in the midst of your land that YHWH your Elohim is giving you. And if it expands (in time to come) you shall add for yourself three more cities beyond these three. And concerning the three cities that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him in 'These are the journeys' to make in Transjordan — he did not mention there, nor did Moshe command Israel; therefore it is written here, for Moshe had already set them apart, and that is why he did not command Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:21.159146084Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}